CREATE TABLE tn (id int NOT NULL, g int, v int, w int, u int) WITH (autovacuum_enabled = false);
INSERT INTO tn SELECT i, i % 20, (i * 31) % 97, i % 13, CASE WHEN i % 7 = 1 THEN NULL ELSE i % 400 END FROM generate_series(1, 4000) i;
CREATE INDEX tn_col ON tn USING sift_col (id, g, v, w, u);
NOTICE:  sift_col index "tn_col": rollup_dims = 'auto' writes a rollup of the rows by g, w
DETAIL:  A GROUP BY or a filter of both columns is read from the cells of each unit. Their combinations fit the cells a unit may keep (a tenth of its rows, at most 4096) in at least 90% of 1 sampled stretches of about a unit, about 260 of them a unit; the cells add to the index and to its build.
HINT:  To drop it, run ALTER INDEX tn_col SET (rollup_dims = 'off') and REINDEX; rollup_dims = 'a, b: measure' names the columns.
